The close6 lock leak is fixed in the real lifecycle replays: TERM after sink startup returned 143 and freed the lock; a detached child inherited no lock descriptor. Normal release was immediate, and SIGKILL released the lease in about 0.49 seconds.

Two publication races remain. Recovery can use a stale preflight scan, or a launcher can die after spawning its child but before recording `child.pid`. I reproduced both with stub children; in each case, recovery could promote another attempt of the same arm while the child remained alive.
